DESCRIPTION >
    Materializes the `deductions` array on `events` into per-balance hourly rows.

    ARRAY JOIN over JSONExtractArrayRaw(toString(deductions), 'list') fans one event out to one row
    per deduction — normally 1:1, max 3 observed in prod. Events with an empty deduction set produce
    no rows, since ARRAY JOIN over an empty array drops them.

    The double JSONExtractString is not a mistake. `deductions` holds {"list": [...]} where each
    element is a JSON *string* containing the deduction object, so the inner call unwraps the string
    and the outer one reads the field. This is the only place that decode happens; the read pipe
    never touches JSON.

    No properties are carried through — see the datasource description for why.

NODE materialize
SQL >
    SELECT
        org_id,
        env,
        customer_id,
        coalesce(entity_id, '') as entity_id,
        event_name,
        JSONExtractString(JSONExtractString(d), 'feature_id') as balance_feature_id,
        JSONExtractString(JSONExtractString(d), 'balance_id') as balance_id,
        JSONExtractString(JSONExtractString(d), 'plan_id') as plan_id,
        JSONExtractString(
            JSONExtractRaw(JSONExtractString(d), 'reset'),
            'interval'
        ) as reset_interval,
        toStartOfHour(timestamp) as hour,
        sum(JSONExtractFloat(JSONExtractString(d), 'value')) as deducted,
        count() as deduction_count
    FROM events
    ARRAY JOIN JSONExtractArrayRaw(toString(deductions), 'list') as d
    WHERE JSONExtractString(JSONExtractString(d), 'balance_id') != ''
    GROUP BY
        org_id,
        env,
        customer_id,
        entity_id,
        event_name,
        balance_feature_id,
        balance_id,
        plan_id,
        reset_interval,
        hour

TYPE materialized
DATASOURCE events_deductions_hourly_mv
